mode: "100644"
text: "# Examples — growth diagnoses\n\nWorked TikTok diagnoses showing the test-and-expand loop, the broken-phase call, and the routing —\nplus honest expectations. Subject: a solo founder building a SaaS social scheduler. Voice context is\nthe blunt indie-founder voice; your output uses the loaded `voice.md`, `social-strategy.md`,\n`audience.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Diagnosis 1 — \"200 views then it stops\"\n\n**Signals (native analytics):** videos stall at ~200 views; average watch time low; slow intros;\ncompletion well under 70%.\n**Broken stage:** **Phase-1 death.** The video isn't holding the test audience, so it never expands.\n**Prescription:**\n- Rebuild the **1-second hook** (open on the claim/stakes; no \"hey guys\"). → `hook-writer`,\n  `tiktok-script`.\n- Raise **completion** — faster pacing, cut dead air, shorter cut, add a **loop/rewatch trigger**.\n- This is a completion problem, not a followers or volume problem.\n→ Re-check average watch time / completion % in analytics.\n\n## Diagnosis 2 — \"Good views, barely any followers\"\n\n**Signals:** some videos hit 20–50k; follower count crawls; profile is a vague bio; every video is a\none-off with no through-line.\n**Broken stage:** **Follow-conversion.** Cold viewers watch and leave — no reason to follow.\n**Prescription:**\n- Fix the **profile** (3-second test, searchable name, who/what/why, pinned). → `profile-optimization`.\n- Give people a reason to follow: a **Series** (\"Building [Product] — Part N\") so viewers come back\n  for the next episode, and a **consistent niche** so a follow means \"more of this.\"\n→ Track **follows-per-video** and profile visits.\n\n## Diagnosis 3 — \"I rely on the FYP lottery and it's inconsistent\"\n\n**Signals:** reach swings wildly; nothing discoverable between hits; no keywords in captions/audio.\n**Broken stage:** **Search** (missing the evergreen lane) + **volume/consistency.**\n**Prescription:**\n- Build the **search lane**: triple-mention keywords (spoken + on-screen + caption), captions as\n  search queries, keyword clusters. → `hashtag-strategy`/`social-seo`, `tiktok-script`.\n- Sustainable **at-bats** (~3–5×/week, quality-gated) → `content-calendar`; **read patterns** across\n  videos to find repeatable winners → `viral-reverse-engineering`.\n→ Watch the **traffic-source** split (FYP vs Search vs Profile) climb on Search.\n\n---\n\n## Honest expectations (say this)\n\n- **The interest graph is meritocratic but ruthless** — it rewards what the video *does to viewers*,\n  not your follower count or effort. Good news for small accounts; humbling for everyone.\n- **Followers don't buy reach.** Reach is per-video (completion, rewatch, search). Followers are the\n  business asset (LIVE/Shop/owned audience).\n- **One flop is noise.** Judge by patterns across many at-bats; the back-catalog can resurface weeks\n  later.\n- **No hacks, no bought followers, no guarantees** — virality has luck; you stack the odds.\n- **Flux:** the US algorithm is retraining through ~mid-2026 — expect swings; hold to fundamentals.\n- **No WoopSocial analytics** — read native TikTok analytics (needs a business/creator account).\n\n---\n\n## What the diagnoses share\n\n- They name **one broken stage/phase** of the loop, not a tip list.\n- They **route to the specific skill** that fixes it.\n- They center **completion/rewatch**, the **search** lane, and **consistent at-bats**.\n- They treat **followers as a business outcome**, set **honest expectations**, and use **vanity-free\n  metrics**.\n"
